  "body": "### What is the issue with the Fetch Standard?\n\nResponse body size is currently CORS protected. This works well for subresources, but it means that iframes always \"pass\" and supposedly expose those values to resource timing.\n\nIn Blink, response body size is hidden for cross-origin iframes or for iframes with opaque redirect tainting (cross-origin redirects).\n\nI believe that in WebKit encoded/decoded body size is same-origin anyway.\nSuggesting to align with the implemented reality, which is more secure than the current spec.",
